WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.030
Four speech bubbles float over an island.

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.760
One is a ragged block of prose.

3
00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.470
One is a neat column of verse.

4
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.890
One is full of music notes.

5
00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.090
And one rhymes, line after line.

6
00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:18.270
Two drunken servants stagger
past, chattering in prose.

7
00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.390
Then another figure answers
them: "Be not afeard.

8
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:27.140
The isle is full of noises," So why
does the play keep changing voice?

9
00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:29.870
In this mission, you'll
sort who speaks verse,

10
00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.620
who speaks prose, and who sings.

11
00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:36.430
You'll listen closely to
Caliban's island and its sounds.

12
00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:41.780
And you'll watch a masque of goddesses,
then hear Prospero step out of the play:

13
00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:45.880
"Now my charms are all
o'erthrown," Your mission:

14
00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:48.740
explain why the play keeps changing voice.
